msg.reasoning_content:
Array response spans multiple lines — my roundTrip helper compares the first response line with the entire multi-line "want". I designed roundTrip to read len(wantLines) lines, but I was passing a multi-line string as a single line. Fix: split want into lines — roundTrip accepts the full response text and compares the concatenated lines. Better helper: roundTrip sends the request and reads until it gets the exact complete expected response (concatenated). Since each response is terminated by a newline, I can read lines and compare the accumulation: read lines until strings.Join(got) == want.

Rewriting roundTrip:
```go
func (cl *client) roundTrip(t *testing.T, in, want string) {
	t.Helper()
	if _, err := cl.c.Write([]byte(in + "\n")); err != nil { t.Fatal(err) }
	acc := ""
	deadline := 5s
	cl.c.SetReadDeadline(time.Now().Add(5*time.Second))
	for !strings.HasSuffix(acc, "\n") || acc != want {
		line, err := cl.r.ReadString('\n')
		if err != nil { t.Fatalf("reading response %q: %v (got so far %q)", in, err, acc) }
		acc += line
		if acc == want { break }
	}
}
```
Simpler loop: keep reading lines and appending, break when acc == want, and error out if err. Then update all call sites: pass a single want string (multi-line is also OK). Call sites currently pass "…\n" strings — just a signature change from ...string to string; the call sites remain valid.

